3. Major Architecture Components
A. Presentation Layer
The frontend provides the interface through which users specify their legal-document requirements.

Responsibilities:

User registration/login

Document-type selection

Collection of party information

Collection of terms and conditions

Effective and termination dates

Clause selection

Document preview

Editing generated content

Download/export

Example input:

Document Type: Non-Disclosure Agreement

Party A: ABC Technologies Pvt. Ltd.
Party B: XYZ Solutions Pvt. Ltd.

Effective Date: 01/10/2026
Term: 2 years

Confidential Information:
- Business information
- Technical information
- Customer information

Governing Law: India

B. Backend/API Layer
The backend acts as the central controller between the frontend, database, AI model, and document-generation services.

Responsibilities:

Authenticate users

Validate incoming data

Store document metadata

Construct AI requests

Communicate with Gemini

Validate AI responses

Handle errors

Generate documents

Maintain document versions

Frontend
   ↓
REST API / Backend
   ↓
Validation
   ↓
AI Service
   ↓
Document Service

C. AI/LLM Service
This is the core Generative AI component.

Selected Model: Gemini 2.5 Pro

LegalEase sends structured user requirements to Gemini using a carefully designed prompt.

The AI service should include:

System prompt

Document-specific instructions

User-provided information

Legal template/context where applicable

Output schema

Safety and validation rules

The application should not simply ask the model to "write a legal document." Instead, it should constrain the expected output.

For example:

Generate an NDA using the supplied parties, dates,
confidentiality requirements and governing law.

Return the result according to the specified JSON schema.

Required sections:
1. Parties
2. Definitions
3. Confidentiality Obligations
4. Exclusions
5. Term
6. Termination
7. Governing Law
8. Signatures

4. Structured AI Output
LegalEase should use structured output rather than depending entirely on unstructured text.

Example:

{
  "documentType": "NDA",
  "title": "NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "ABC Technologies Pvt. Ltd.",
      "role": "Disclosing Party"
    },
    {
      "name": "XYZ Solutions Pvt. Ltd.",
      "role": "Receiving Party"
    }
  ],
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-01",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Confidentiality",
      "content": "..."
    },
    {
      "title": "Term",
      "content": "..."
    },
    {
      "title": "Governing Law",
      "content": "..."
    }
  ]
}

This makes it easier for the backend to validate and format the generated document.

